OL,3,GNEWSAPolish ambassador joins WW2 plaque
OL,4,Aunveiling
OL,5,
OL,6,FA blue plaque has been unveiled at a
OL,7,Fpub in Oxfordshire in memory of polish
OL,8,Fsoldiers and their families that
OL,9,Fsettled nearby after the second world
OL,10,Fwar.
OL,12,FThe Black Horse Pub in Checkendon was a
OL,13,Fhub for hundreds of Poles who lived in
OL,14,Fwoodland refugee camps in Checkendon,
OL,15,FNettlebed and Highmoor from 1946-1961.
OL,17,FAfter the war the Soviets had occupied
OL,18,FPoland, so many Poles that fought
OL,19,Falongside the British started new lives
OL,20,Fin Oxfordshire because they were unable
OL,21,Fto return home.
OL,23,APub: 12-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
